{"item_id": "791", "buckets": {"question_type": "free_form", "answer_type": "float", "task": "textbook question answering"}, "score_status": "scored", "correct": true, "extracted": "1.06", "normalized": "1.06", "gold": "1.06", "response": "Treat \\(R_L\\) as a load connected across the bridge’s Thevenin equivalent.\n\n\\[\nV_A=5\\left(\\frac{R_2}{R_1+R_2}\\right)=5\\left(\\frac{2.2}{1+2.2}\\right)=3.4375\\text{ V}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nV_B=5\\left(\\frac{R_4}{R_3+R_4}\\right)=5\\left(\\frac{1.5}{2.2+1.5}\\right)=2.0270\\text{ V}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nV_{\\text{th}}=V_A-V_B=1.4105\\text{ V}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nR_{\\text{th}}=(R_1\\parallel R_2)+(R_3\\parallel R_4)\n=0.6875+0.8919=1.5794\\text{ k}\\Omega\n\\]\n\nThe current through \\(R_L\\) is\n\n\\[\nI_L=\\frac{V_{\\text{th}}}{R_{\\text{th}}+R_L}\n=\\frac{1.4105}{1.5794+4.7}\n=0.2246\\text{ mA}\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\nV_L=I_LR_L=(0.2246\\text{ mA})(4.7\\text{ k}\\Omega)=1.0557\\text{ V}\n\\]\n\nThe polarity is positive at \\(A\\) relative to \\(B\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1.06\\text{ V}}\n\\]"}
