{"item_id": "862", "buckets": {"question_type": "free_form", "answer_type": "float", "task": "textbook question answering"}, "score_status": "scored", "correct": false, "extracted": "The launch velocity is **10.44 m/s**, and the landing velocity is **19.53 m/s**.\n\n**19.53**", "normalized": null, "gold": "10.44", "response": "Ignoring air resistance, the horizontal velocity is constant:\n\n\\[\nv_{0x}=\\frac{D}{t}=\\frac{20.0}{2.50}=8.00\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\nThus the launch speed is\n\n\\[\nv_0=\\frac{v_{0x}}{\\cos\\theta_0}\n=\\frac{8.00}{\\cos 40.0^\\circ}\n=10.44\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\nThe initial vertical component is\n\n\\[\nv_{0y}=v_{0x}\\tan40.0^\\circ=6.71\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\nAt landing,\n\n\\[\nv_y=v_{0y}-gt=6.71-(9.81)(2.50)=-17.81\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\nv_{\\text{landing}}\n=\\sqrt{v_x^2+v_y^2}\n=\\sqrt{8.00^2+(-17.81)^2}\n=19.53\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{v_0=10.44\\ \\text{m/s},\\qquad v_{\\text{landing}}=19.53\\ \\text{m/s}}\n\\]"}
